%% HANDWRITTEN. Checked against ARCHITECTURE.md S6 + D37 + D14 + config/menus.yaml
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Customer
    participant TEL as Telephony
    participant IVR as IVR service
    participant PACK as DomainPack
    participant ORCH as CallOrchestrator

    C->>TEL: dials +6621234000 (general hotline)
    TEL->>IVR: call arrives, ANI +66898887777
    IVR->>PACK: did("+6621234000")
    PACK-->>IVR: line unknown, skip_product_menu false

    Note over IVR,C: STEP 1 - which product line?
    IVR->>C: "กด 1 ประกันรถยนต์ กด 2 ประกันสุขภาพ ..."
    Note right of IVR: reordered if we recognise them, but it<br/>NEVER speaks their details aloud (D37)
    C->>IVR: presses 2

    Note over IVR,C: STEP 2 - why are you calling?
    IVR->>C: "กด 1 แจ้งเข้ารักษาผู้ป่วยใน ... กด 4 สอบถามความคุ้มครอง ..."
    C->>IVR: presses 4

    IVR->>PACK: walk_menu(["2","4"])
    PACK-->>IVR: line health, intent health.coverage.query
    IVR->>PACK: queue_for_intent - intent to skill to queue
    PACK-->>IVR: q_health_policy

    Note over IVR,ORCH: ROUTING IS NOW SETTLED. No AI has run. (D37)

    IVR->>C: "ให้บันทึกเสียงเพื่อเตรียมข้อมูลไหมคะ กด 1 ตกลง กด 2 ไม่"
    alt presses 1
        C->>IVR: 1
        IVR->>ORCH: record_consent(recording + ai_processing)
        ORCH-->>IVR: intake may run
    else presses 2, or says nothing
        C->>IVR: 2
        IVR->>ORCH: no consent recorded
        Note right of ORCH: the call proceeds anyway (D14). The brief<br/>stays context-only - and is still correctly routed.
    end
    ORCH->>ORCH: enqueue(q_health_policy)
